WEBVTT

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:01.790
Joonsang is fine,

00:00:01.790 --> 00:00:03.560
so don't ever call me again.

00:00:04.020 --> 00:00:06.730
<i>Is it true that Joonsang is our son?</i>

00:00:07.980 --> 00:00:08.980
<i>Is it?</i>

00:00:10.900 --> 00:00:11.900
<i>Is it?</i>

00:00:16.330 --> 00:00:18.550
No, Joonsang is <i>my</i> son.

00:00:18.550 --> 00:00:20.740
He's <i>my</i> only son.

00:00:23.540 --> 00:00:24.420
H-Honey...

00:00:29.170 --> 00:00:31.510
How could you?!

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:33.470
How could you cheat on me?!

00:00:36.390 --> 00:00:37.220
Honey!

00:00:39.470 --> 00:00:40.220
Honey!

00:00:41.430 --> 00:00:42.480
Honey!

00:00:42.480 --> 00:00:43.810
Get a hold of yourself!

00:02:38.760 --> 00:02:39.630
Mother.

00:02:41.020 --> 00:02:42.880
Could you leave the room?

00:02:42.880 --> 00:02:44.640
I'd like to be alone.

00:02:57.350 --> 00:02:58.280
Sanghyuk.

00:02:59.740 --> 00:03:00.700
Sanghyuk.

00:03:03.820 --> 00:03:06.080
I'm not going to ask you to forgive me.

00:03:07.000 --> 00:03:10.250
There's probably nothing I can say to you that could absolve me.

00:03:12.270 --> 00:03:13.460
But Joonsang is...

00:03:14.710 --> 00:03:16.140
Go ahead and talk.

00:03:16.140 --> 00:03:17.840
I'll hear anything you have to offer.

00:03:18.510 --> 00:03:19.550
About Joonsang...

00:03:20.630 --> 00:03:22.550
please don't hate him for this.

00:03:22.720 --> 00:03:25.600
He's the biggest victim of us all.

00:03:28.720 --> 00:03:29.930
You want to talk about victims?

00:03:30.620 --> 00:03:31.830
What about Mother?

00:03:31.830 --> 00:03:32.350
What about me?

00:03:33.480 --> 00:03:35.770
I trusted you for the last twenty-eight years of my life.

00:03:36.980 --> 00:03:37.860
I really did.

00:03:45.870 --> 00:03:48.370
He seems to be in critical condition.

00:03:48.870 --> 00:03:51.120
Shouldn't we tell Yujin about it?

00:03:55.470 --> 00:03:57.420
I'm really sorry to ask you to do this,

00:03:57.420 --> 00:03:59.050
but could you call Yujin—

00:04:10.390 --> 00:04:12.310
How could you not have seen him leave?

00:04:12.390 --> 00:04:13.640
W-Well...

00:04:13.940 --> 00:04:15.650
Call security.

00:04:16.910 --> 00:04:17.580
Yes, Doctor.

00:04:18.230 --> 00:04:20.280
Tell them to search the premises first.

00:04:37.110 --> 00:04:38.130
Are you sure you're all right with this?

00:04:39.540 --> 00:04:40.900
Well, it's not like I have a choice, right?

00:04:40.900 --> 00:04:43.840
You said you're not going to have the surgery until you get this done.

00:04:45.010 --> 00:04:47.680
The least I can do is stay by your side and keep an eye on you.

00:04:48.620 --> 00:04:51.100
I can't just abandon my patient now, can I?

00:04:54.230 --> 00:04:56.440
Your loft is in this neighborhood somewhere, right?

00:04:56.440 --> 00:04:57.270
Yeah.

00:04:57.900 --> 00:04:59.110
Could we get out here?

00:05:07.990 --> 00:05:10.090
You don't mind if we ditch what you have to do for a bit

00:05:10.090 --> 00:05:12.120
and go on a little walk, do you?

00:05:26.590 --> 00:05:28.510
You stubborn old man!

00:05:28.640 --> 00:05:30.050
Could you please leave now?

00:05:34.850 --> 00:05:36.440
Start on it right away!

00:05:36.810 --> 00:05:38.560
Like I've told you; I refuse.

00:05:40.710 --> 00:05:42.400
Oh Dear Father in Heaven...

00:05:50.590 --> 00:05:52.330
Do you work here?

00:05:52.950 --> 00:05:55.580
N-No, not yet;

00:05:55.580 --> 00:05:57.120
I'm trying to get a job here, though.

00:06:00.210 --> 00:06:02.000
Make sure Claude gets that.

00:06:02.500 --> 00:06:05.510
Tell him that restoring the Basilica of St. Thérèse is a calling, not a job.

00:06:06.750 --> 00:06:10.430
It is He who chooses who should work.

00:06:16.520 --> 00:06:18.060
Wait!

00:06:20.020 --> 00:06:22.110
Wait, what am I supposed to do with—

00:06:39.960 --> 00:06:43.250
Why on earth are you interested in restorative architecture?

00:06:44.130 --> 00:06:47.380
And why would you rather learn it on-site and not at some school?

00:06:48.050 --> 00:06:50.630
With nothing but minor renovation experience, at that.

00:06:55.600 --> 00:06:57.940
Either say something or leave.

00:06:57.940 --> 00:06:59.310
I have work to do.

00:07:01.310 --> 00:07:05.480
"There is much more effort involved in restoration than building anew;

00:07:06.440 --> 00:07:08.930
that is because one must first understand the emotions and memories

00:07:08.930 --> 00:07:10.650
of the place he wishes to restore.

00:07:12.070 --> 00:07:14.410
What separates restoration from simple maintenance work,

00:07:14.530 --> 00:07:18.370
is that one can pour one's heart and time into restoration."

00:07:19.160 --> 00:07:21.790
That's what your book said.

00:07:23.030 --> 00:07:25.130
That book must have done pretty well.

00:07:25.750 --> 00:07:26.500
So,

00:07:27.630 --> 00:07:29.670
are you here to brag about your good memory, then?

00:07:29.920 --> 00:07:33.430
I want to build a house that I can pour my heart into,

00:07:33.550 --> 00:07:35.140
but I don't know how to do it.

00:07:38.510 --> 00:07:39.310
Aren't you...

00:07:40.680 --> 00:07:43.980
I want to learn how I can pour my heart,

00:07:44.710 --> 00:07:46.730
and engrave my memories,

00:07:47.900 --> 00:07:49.320
into something I'm building.

00:07:59.530 --> 00:08:00.790
Don't you remember me?

00:08:18.740 --> 00:08:20.430
Don't worry, I'm okay.

00:08:20.890 --> 00:08:22.480
I'm not.

00:08:25.150 --> 00:08:28.480
These heels are a little too high to be going on walks in.

00:08:34.400 --> 00:08:38.370
"Without me there is no you, and without you there is no me"?

00:08:40.910 --> 00:08:45.000
We used to walk around reading all the message plates here.

00:08:45.720 --> 00:08:46.670
Did we?

00:08:47.380 --> 00:08:49.250
Do you remember Ms. Queenie?

00:08:52.800 --> 00:08:56.590
She always used to stumble around here because she forgot

00:08:56.720 --> 00:08:59.760
where the message plate her husband made for her was, remember?

00:09:02.140 --> 00:09:02.870
I remember now.

00:09:02.870 --> 00:09:05.890
We even drew a sign to the bench so that she'd remember.

00:09:07.100 --> 00:09:08.860
That bench should be around here somewhere, too.

00:09:11.610 --> 00:09:12.730
So you do remember.

00:09:14.870 --> 00:09:16.240
It's this bench.

00:09:18.410 --> 00:09:21.280
"Humans build houses because they are alive.

00:09:21.410 --> 00:09:25.330
However, they are writing because they know they will die."

00:09:26.120 --> 00:09:30.040
I thought of this message when I first heard that you'd become an architect.

00:09:31.670 --> 00:09:33.380
I'd forgotten all that.

00:09:34.240 --> 00:09:37.340
Don't you think those forgotten memories of the past

00:09:37.760 --> 00:09:39.760
are what shapes our perceptions of today?

00:09:44.320 --> 00:09:46.810
It used to feel like we were on a treasure hunt

00:09:46.810 --> 00:09:49.770
when the three of us took turns

00:09:49.900 --> 00:09:52.070
making the other two guess which bench we wanted them to find.

00:09:53.020 --> 00:09:54.760
It's all coming back to me now.

00:09:54.760 --> 00:09:56.650
I can remember it as if it happened yesterday.

00:09:58.410 --> 00:10:00.990
Both you, and Harry...

00:10:02.990 --> 00:10:05.580
It's probably those memories that called me back here,

00:10:06.960 --> 00:10:09.500
and let us meet one another again.

00:10:10.670 --> 00:10:12.960
But why at the hospital, right?

00:10:13.500 --> 00:10:14.420
Yeah.

00:10:15.960 --> 00:10:17.090
I didn't understand back then

00:10:17.720 --> 00:10:20.200
that you could have feelings for another that you'd want to express so much

00:10:20.200 --> 00:10:21.850
that you'd even go so far as engrave them on a bench like this.

00:10:22.560 --> 00:10:23.850
Do you understand it now?

00:10:24.220 --> 00:10:25.100
Maybe.

00:10:26.430 --> 00:10:28.230
I have my own bench here too.

00:10:29.230 --> 00:10:29.850
Wanna look for it?

00:10:43.700 --> 00:10:46.080
It feels like I'm on a treasure hunt again.

00:10:47.870 --> 00:10:48.710
Do I get a prize if I find it?

00:10:48.960 --> 00:10:50.170
Of course.

00:11:06.390 --> 00:11:09.480
It's the puzzle you were solving with Harry, isn't it.

00:11:09.980 --> 00:11:12.150
I couldn't understand it either.

00:11:12.600 --> 00:11:14.600
I didn't get why anyone would want to leave someone a message

00:11:14.600 --> 00:11:16.320
knowing that they'll never get it.

00:11:17.280 --> 00:11:19.820
But I think I understand it now.

00:11:20.280 --> 00:11:22.780
Your memory lives on, so long as there's someone remembering it for you.

00:11:23.240 --> 00:11:24.780
You were talking about the "Impossible House," weren't you?

00:11:25.580 --> 00:11:26.820
You said that

00:11:26.820 --> 00:11:29.290
"a loving heart is the best home two loving people could have," right?

00:11:29.870 --> 00:11:32.140
If you truly want to show that you believe it,

00:11:32.140 --> 00:11:34.630
you can't give up.

00:11:36.000 --> 00:11:37.210
Just give it a thought.

00:11:37.210 --> 00:11:39.710
Think about what you'd need if you were to build a house

00:11:39.800 --> 00:11:41.170
that she truly wants to live in.

00:11:50.960 --> 00:11:53.350
You said there's something you have to do while you can still see, right?

00:11:54.250 --> 00:11:56.570
I think this is something you should see through,

00:11:56.570 --> 00:11:59.400
even if you should lose your vision.

00:12:00.320 --> 00:12:03.820
Even if <i>you</i> were to lose your memories because of the operation,

00:12:05.370 --> 00:12:07.370
I'm sure <i>she</i> would remember you.

00:12:14.880 --> 00:12:15.790
Joonsang?

00:12:16.600 --> 00:12:18.500
Where are you, Joonsang?

00:12:19.420 --> 00:12:21.550
It looks like even the winter sky is gone.

00:12:22.750 --> 00:12:25.090
I really liked the winter sky.

00:12:25.880 --> 00:12:27.970
I guess I won't be able to see this sky anymore.

00:12:29.120 --> 00:12:31.310
I'm going to the airport.

00:12:32.140 --> 00:12:33.560
Take care of Yujin for me.

00:12:34.440 --> 00:12:36.020
<i>Make sure to look after her,</i>

00:12:36.810 --> 00:12:39.860
<i>so that she won't feel sad or troubled.</i>

00:12:40.400 --> 00:12:41.280
Joonsang...

00:12:41.400 --> 00:12:42.540
<i>Please.</i>

00:12:42.540 --> 00:12:44.540
<i>I'm asking you from the bottom of my heart.</i>

00:12:44.540 --> 00:12:45.780
<i>I'm not going to be coming back.</i>

00:12:45.910 --> 00:12:46.470
Joonsang.

00:12:46.470 --> 00:12:47.030
Joonsang!

00:12:48.990 --> 00:12:49.910
<i>Friends?</i>

00:12:50.790 --> 00:12:53.500
<i>So we're finally friends?</i>

00:12:55.170 --> 00:12:56.500
<i>And it turned out to be so easy.</i>

00:12:58.330 --> 00:13:00.800
<i>Why do you think it was so hard for us</i>

00:13:01.550 --> 00:13:03.340
<i>to take things one step at a time back then?</i>

00:13:11.940 --> 00:13:12.850
<i>Hello?</i>

00:13:19.440 --> 00:13:20.570
Could you take his BP for me?

00:13:21.150 --> 00:13:22.820
Yes, Doctor.

00:13:25.240 --> 00:13:27.320
We'll start the surgery as soon as he's anesthetized.

00:13:27.710 --> 00:13:29.200
Checking vital signs one last time.

00:13:29.320 --> 00:13:30.780
Yes, we're all set here.

00:13:31.080 --> 00:13:33.370
Now, take a deep breath.

00:13:34.050 --> 00:13:35.210
And let it out.

00:13:48.130 --> 00:13:52.390
You're not mistaking Joonsang for your dead brother Harry now, are you?

00:13:54.760 --> 00:13:56.770
It'll be hard for you to perform surgery

00:13:56.770 --> 00:13:58.980
if you're indeed harboring personal feelings for him.

00:13:59.480 --> 00:14:01.710
It's not too late;

00:14:01.710 --> 00:14:03.480
I can have a different surgeon take over, if you'd like.

00:14:04.360 --> 00:14:06.900
I'm his doctor and his surgeon.

00:14:07.960 --> 00:14:10.160
He's just a patient, nothing more.

00:14:11.530 --> 00:14:13.990
I trust I can take your word on this.

00:14:25.420 --> 00:14:27.220
Harry!

00:14:27.800 --> 00:14:29.140
No!

00:14:32.600 --> 00:14:33.440
It's okay.

00:14:33.440 --> 00:14:35.270
It'll be fine.

00:14:35.450 --> 00:14:38.980
What if Harry dies?

00:14:45.790 --> 00:14:47.780
He'll be all right, won't he?

00:14:48.400 --> 00:14:50.410
Yeah, he'll be fine.

00:14:56.450 --> 00:14:57.330
<i>Harry...</i>

00:14:57.790 --> 00:15:00.620
<i>I know you're watching. Give me strength.</i>

00:15:01.120 --> 00:15:02.790
<i>I can't let him die like this.</i>

00:15:03.670 --> 00:15:04.590
Scalpel.

00:15:05.130 --> 00:15:06.000
Scalpel.

00:15:18.790 --> 00:15:20.060
Please, Joonsang...

00:15:23.020 --> 00:15:26.070
Don't worry so much. Take a seat over there.

00:15:30.360 --> 00:15:32.070
This will be the last time.

00:15:33.030 --> 00:15:34.530
The last time?

00:15:35.790 --> 00:15:37.410
You'll never see me again.

00:15:39.810 --> 00:15:44.580
You told me once, when I asked about my father, that he's dead, right?

00:15:46.670 --> 00:15:51.130
You'll answer the same way whenever someone asks you about me.

00:16:12.860 --> 00:16:13.950
Hey, Mi Hee!

00:16:14.780 --> 00:16:16.700
Get a grip, Mi Hee!

00:16:27.170 --> 00:16:29.670
<i>You have reached the voice mailbox of...</i>

00:16:42.070 --> 00:16:43.190
I'm sorry.

00:16:43.190 --> 00:16:45.440
The Sister insisted I give it to you.

00:16:45.550 --> 00:16:47.110
I didn't think it'd be brandy.

00:16:47.850 --> 00:16:51.360
There's more inside this bottle than just brandy.

00:16:51.940 --> 00:16:54.920
She told me to tell you that

00:16:54.920 --> 00:16:57.910
"restoring the Basilica of St. Thérèse is a calling, not a job,"

00:16:57.910 --> 00:16:59.620
and that "it is He who chooses who should work."

00:17:00.240 --> 00:17:02.750
So "<i>He</i> chooses who should work," huh?

00:17:24.140 --> 00:17:25.480
Would you like a drink?

00:17:26.810 --> 00:17:28.230
Oh, I can't drink alcohol.

00:17:28.400 --> 00:17:31.100
I was out for an entire day the last time

00:17:31.100 --> 00:17:33.440
when all I had was a glass of mulled wine when I had a cold.

00:17:35.070 --> 00:17:38.950
So is this the Basilica of St. Thérèse of Lisieux?

00:17:39.870 --> 00:17:41.410
It's a beautiful place.

00:17:41.780 --> 00:17:44.160
Would you like to be in charge of restoring it?

00:17:45.540 --> 00:17:46.550
Me?

00:17:46.550 --> 00:17:47.420
How could I...

00:17:47.560 --> 00:17:50.040
You wouldn't be able to do it right away, of course.

00:17:50.420 --> 00:17:52.630
Even my apprentices end up working with me

00:17:52.750 --> 00:17:55.310
for at least six to seven years

00:17:55.310 --> 00:17:57.800
before they can stand on their own two feet.

00:17:58.430 --> 00:17:59.760
But the restoration work on the basilica

00:17:59.760 --> 00:18:01.680
needs to start within the next three years.

00:18:02.350 --> 00:18:04.930
Then it'd be impossible for me to do it.

00:18:05.020 --> 00:18:07.890
But if you really are as passionate as you seem,

00:18:07.980 --> 00:18:12.650
then you should be able to learn it much faster than the rest.

00:18:15.320 --> 00:18:17.240
It's like the Sister said.

00:18:18.130 --> 00:18:21.990
If restoring the Basilica of St. Thérèse is indeed my calling,

00:18:22.770 --> 00:18:24.460
then they probably won't be able to find

00:18:24.460 --> 00:18:26.750
anyone else to work on it before me.

00:18:27.350 --> 00:18:30.750
But that doesn't guarantee that they'll hold out for you.

00:18:31.080 --> 00:18:33.170
Oh ye of little faith.

00:18:33.170 --> 00:18:35.590
That Sister is stubborn, I guarantee it;

00:18:36.010 --> 00:18:40.380
but I have no intention of working on the basilica.

00:18:40.510 --> 00:18:44.930
I will, however, lend you my name so that you can work on it someday.

00:18:45.640 --> 00:18:47.180
Why would you do that for me?

00:18:49.530 --> 00:18:51.310
I believe in fate.

00:18:51.890 --> 00:18:53.880
If you empty this glass of Calvados,

00:18:53.880 --> 00:18:56.110
I'll take it that you've accepted my offer.

00:18:56.280 --> 00:18:58.030
I can't drink alcohol.

00:18:59.970 --> 00:19:01.700
Fate is often cruel, you know.

00:19:10.960 --> 00:19:12.290
To Joan.

00:19:22.760 --> 00:19:24.100
To Joan.

00:20:00.880 --> 00:20:01.880
Joonsang.

00:20:03.590 --> 00:20:04.320
<i>I...</i>

00:20:05.780 --> 00:20:07.640
<i>I couldn't keep our promise.</i>

00:20:10.220 --> 00:20:11.600
<i>I was there</i>

00:20:13.310 --> 00:20:16.520
<i>on the day you left.</i>

00:20:26.740 --> 00:20:27.700
<i>Yujin.</i>

00:20:28.660 --> 00:20:31.200
<i>I know we promised that we wouldn't look back.</i>

00:20:32.660 --> 00:20:36.630
<i>And that our backs wouldn't be the last thing we'd see of each other...</i>

00:20:38.660 --> 00:20:41.050
<i>I'm sorry, Yujin.</i>

00:21:52.290 --> 00:21:53.410
Your heart's been broken by someone.

00:21:58.040 --> 00:21:59.420
Your man left you.

00:22:07.590 --> 00:22:09.050
I can see him.

00:22:09.340 --> 00:22:11.030
He may be alive, but he's not really alive;

00:22:11.030 --> 00:22:12.680
he may be dead, but he's not really dead.

00:22:18.920 --> 00:22:20.190
Pick a card.

00:22:29.160 --> 00:22:30.070
What is this?

00:22:32.200 --> 00:22:33.950
It's a scary picture.

00:22:34.870 --> 00:22:36.500
It's a special card.

00:22:36.870 --> 00:22:40.500
It's card XIII, which many call "the nameless secret".

00:22:41.130 --> 00:22:43.040
Is it supposed to be bad?

00:22:43.460 --> 00:22:46.710
One could certainly think so, because the card is called "Death".

00:22:47.240 --> 00:22:50.930
However, this card does not signify an end, but a new beginning.

00:22:51.390 --> 00:22:54.250
Here, take this and start anew,

00:22:54.250 --> 00:22:55.970
like you did when you first met him.

00:22:57.100 --> 00:22:58.770
When I first met him?

00:23:07.150 --> 00:23:08.740
The ticket inspector's coming!

00:23:12.570 --> 00:23:13.950
Come on, Mom.

00:23:14.950 --> 00:23:15.870
This way.
